  "workspace": "The Casely Group",
  "botUser": "U0AUPGF8GRF",
  "channel": "D***07U3",
  "anchorTs": "1783640151.091679",
  "threadProgressChrome": {
    "input": ":hammer_and_wrench: `pnpm test`",
    "result": {
      "messageId": "suppressed",
      "suppressed": true
    },
    "anchorReactionNames": ["hammer_and_wrench"]
  },
  "noThreadProgressChrome": {
    "input": ":writing_hand: Write: MEMORY.md",
    "result": {
      "messageId": "suppressed",
      "suppressed": true
    }
  },
  "semanticReply": {
    "input": ":hammer_and_wrench: I ran `pnpm test` and it passed",
    "result": {
      "messageId": "1783640151.421249",
      "suppressed": false,
      "threadTs": "1783640151.091679"
    }
  },
  "redactedThreadTranscript": [
    {
      "ts": "1783640151.091679",
      "text": "Slack progress-chrome guard live proof anchor 2026-07-09T23:35:50.946Z",
      "reactions": ["hammer_and_wrench"]
    },
    {
      "ts": "1783640151.421249",
      "text": ":hammer_and_wrench: I ran `pnpm test` and it passed",
      "reactions": null
    }
  ]
}
```

## Verification
- Thread-scoped progress chrome converts to `reactions.add` instead of `chat.postMessage`.
- Progress chrome without a reaction target is suppressed before Slack post.
- Semantic replies using the same leading emoji and an embedded backticked command remain sendable, including without final sentence punctuation.

